Description: Rust libraries used by Telegram Desktop
 Telegram Desktop 7.3 links all of its Rust dependencies as a single static
 library, tdesktop_rust, so that one copy of the Rust standard library, its
 allocator and its panic machinery serve all of them. It holds:
 .
  * tlottie, the Lottie renderer behind stickers, emoji and interface
    animations, which replaced the bundled rlottie in 7.2.7;
  * wallet-engine, the TON wallet and TON Connect engine behind the in-app
    wallet, with the C++ binding UniFFI generates for it.
 .
 No distribution ships either library, and Telegram Desktop's CMake looks them
 up unconditionally on Linux, so they have to exist as a package before
 telegram-desktop can build.
 .
 This package provides the static library, the tlottie header and the
 wallet-engine binding, whose wallet_engine.cpp Telegram Desktop compiles
 itself. The archive embeds the Rust standard library, so nothing links it at
 runtime. It supersedes libtlottie-dev.
